// lexdb over TNS: the audit's cheap statement forms in the Oracle door (design/lexdb-new-features.md): 26ai's GROUP BY ALL (O7,
// every select item without an aggregate or a window call, *, t.*, HAVING, windows, ORA-03048 / ORA-03049 / ORA-00979), 23ai's
// direct joins in DELETE ([FROM] t [alias] FROM ...) and UPDATE (O9), 26ai's INSERT ... SET and BY NAME / BY POSITION (O10, and
// their errors: ORA-00957, 00904, 00947, 00913, 63875-63878), VALUES as a CTE's body (O5's WITH: ORA-63803, 63801, 63815) and
// DEFAULT ON NULL [FOR INSERT ONLY | FOR INSERT AND UPDATE] (O20: INSERT, INSERT ... SELECT, UPDATE, MERGE, USER_TAB_COLUMNS,
// ORA-01407, 02000, 00936, 30665). Checked against Oracle Database Free 23.26 (gen_oracle.py --check tns_stmtforms: the answers
// below are Oracle's). Each statement runs with set lexdb_batch = off (the row engine) and on: "same" and the answer, or
// DIFFERENT and both; "a ;; b" in a transaction rolled back.
// expect: setup: 28 statements
// expect: same: A,N = 1|2;2|1;NULL|1
